# Ordering asks which of two things comes first, and an effect has no place in
# a sequence until it runs. Equality refuses the same pair for its own reason —
# asking whether two effects are the same effect is asking which one you were
# handed — so the two refusals read differently on purpose.
# The check refuses a provable box here now (the errors corpus pins that
# sentence), so the box travels through a list, where nothing can prove it.
import "std/io"

w = (push [] (io/write "x"))[1]!

pub play = print "{w < w}"
